    <code code="11450-4" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Problem List"/>
    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Recurrent transient episodes of collapse: six days ago a witnessed collapse with stiffening and jerking of both arms for about a minute, a bitten tongue, and about twenty minutes of confusion, after a rising strange feeling and dizziness; two briefer spells of staring and unresponsiveness in the past eighteen months; cause not yet known (seizure, convulsive syncope, or transient ischemic attack)</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R56.9</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to the documented accounts of falling attacks and fainting fits; it resolves when the cause is found.</td>
  </tr>
